# The cut of docs/design.md, section 4: the relay client of
# crates/podssh-relay/src (the hosts, the pool, the rank, the failover, the
# tokens, the roads to a relay, the forward layer, the pairs, the exchange
# of a pairing by code, the grants, the reverse road and the blocking
# facade). lib.rs is the root of the crate. Of cache.rs, the token entries
# come; its private files are pod-core's files (with cache/, which has no
# token or pool part: no file of cache/ comes). Of code/, exchange.rs and
# run.rs come (pod-wormhole has the rest; mod.rs, the choice of the
# mailboxes, stays in podssh). tls_groups.rs stays in podssh: it gives
# pod-tls the file of the cache. podssh-ws h2_road/ and cleartext/ are
# podssh's glue over pod-ws (the pool of the process, the way of a proxy
# choice): no file comes, and the pool is a value of the caller here.
# Of the tests: each test of these files that needs no other module of
# podssh-relay (serve/, quick/ and the other roads), with its harness;
# cleanup/ is pod-core's too. Of tests/cache.rs, the tests of the tokens
# (pod-core has the tests of the files). tests/pair_code.rs and
# pair_code_live.rs: the tests that run an exchange (pod-wormhole has the
# rest). session_relay_resume.rs, relay_serve_*.rs, reverse_carrier.rs,
# reverse_restart.rs and http_road.rs run the relay role (serve/): they go
# with pod-relay-serve. tests/e2e_harness/mod.rs is pod-e2e's adapted copy
# of podssh's harness; tests/mailbox_harness/ is pod-wormhole's harness
# with no peer (podssh's ran the role's mailbox), over the stand-in of
# pod-wormhole's feature `standin`; tests/support/ is new.
